It was the same old, same old for Jack Sterbin. Get up in the morning, turn on the lights, and go to the bathroom, except today something a little different happened.

Right as Jack flicked the light switch, a bright spark illuminated the room for a brief moment. Then everything went dark.

Jack slowly tried to open his eyes, his vision blurry.

"Ugh, can't believe I just got knocked out from being electrocuted"

"Thank god I didn't di-"

Just then, he felt a sharp pain coming from the right side of his stomach.

'AHH, what the hell, did I hit something when I got knocked out?'

His vision started clearing, and the first thing he noticed was that he was no longer in his bedroom. Instead, he saw old concrete beneath him, brick walls on either side that he was leaning against, and the darkness of night. 

'What the hell is happening???'

'It isn't morning, nor am I in my bedroom. Did I get kidnapped?'

Just as the thought occurred, another jolt of sharp pain spread across his entire body, originating from his stomach. Jack was unable to move his neck or head, so he slowly moved his eyes down to where the pain was originating. His breath hitched.

"OH FUCK, FUCK FUCK FUCK. WHY AM I BLEEDING SO MUCH?"

Blood was pouring out of the left side of his stomach, where a deep wound could be seen. A pool of blood had already formed around Jack.

Jack tried to move, but he couldn't lift a finger. As he tried to move his hands, he noticed something even stranger. 

'These aren't my hands?'

They were skinny, bony, and longer than Jack's hands had been. He glanced at the rest of his body with only the eye movements he had control over.

'Wait, these aren't my legs, my arms, or my damn body!'

Just then, a deep sleepy feeling washed over Jack as the pain receded and his eyelids became heavier and heavier.

'Fuck! Am I really about to die right now?'

Just then, a golden wheel appeared on top of Jack's head. Even though he couldn't see it, he could sense that the wheel was there.

'NO SHOT, this is the wheel from Mahoraga, signalling the adaptation ability.'

The wheel started turning, slowly completing 1 rotation.

Something inside Jack had changed; somehow he could inherently understand exactly what that change was.

Immune resistance and response to foreign pathogens increased drastically.

'I'm dying over here, and it gives me such a random adaptation. Yep, it's over for me, might as well close my eyes and hope for the best!'

The thought didn't even finish before the wheel completed another rotation. This time something completely different happened.

'My blood can actually clot a lot faster now during open injuries!'

'At least this one's useful; I don't think I'd survive with just these though.'

The wheel continued rotating, each cycle giving Jack a different feeling inside. However, before Jack could analyse exactly what had happened to his body, his eyelids fully closed. Unable to endure the exhaustion, Jack fell into a deep sleep.

The next morning's sunlight crept into the dark alleys. The rays of sunshine hit Jack's closed eyelids, slowly waking him up. Finally, his eyelids opened to see the exact spot he'd been in the night before.

'Shit, I was hoping that was just a dream.'

'I had my suspicions yesterday, but it looks like I really did transmigrate.'

Jack tried to move, but pain shot through his entire body; however, it was nowhere near as bad as yesterday.

'Looks like I can at least stand now.'

Looking around, he noticed he was in a deserted old alley next to a sewage treatment plant.

'I remember that the wheel made several rotations before I passed out. Didn't get a chance to check the goodies.'

'I focused inward, deep into my body. Somehow, I could inherently sense exactly what changes had occurred.'

As Jack focused on his changes, the results astonished him. Besides the two changes from yesterday, the following adaptations had manifested.

Cellular regeneration increased by 5x.

Blood coagulation efficiency increased.

Cellular oxygen delivery efficiency increased.

Overall energy usage efficiency increased.

Improved ability to maintain circulation after injury.

MSTN gene expression reduced by 80%, resulting in rapid and high levels of potential muscle growth.

The body's ability to implement biological changes rapidly resulting from adaptation increased significantly.

Jack felt the long list of adaptations given by Mahoraga's ability and became ecstatic, especially because of the last one.

"FUCKKK YEAAA."

Not used to his voice, it came out raspier than he'd thought.

'Must've been the last ability that actually made the rest useful; otherwise, even if all the other adaptations existed, it would've been too late. But the last ability compresses what could be done in months of bodily changes into mere hours.'

He looked at his hands; they were no longer as gaunt or bony as before.

'Is that why I look slightly more muscular now, even though the MSTN gene modification has only happened for a few hours now?'

Just as his thoughts began to wander, a rush of memories from the original's body came back to him.

It was like watching a movie compressed into a couple of seconds.

However, it wasn't the original body's entire life story, just small tidbits here and there, along with why he had a massive wound, dying in the middle of an alley.

Turns out, the original body's name is also Jack Sterbin and 20 years old. 6 feet tall and unhealthily underweight. But he was a homeless man with advanced cancer, looking for a place to sleep when he stumbled upon a big guy holding a hatchet. The original body tried to get away, hoping he was just a normal guy, but when the big guy turned around, transmigrator Jack understood exactly who the original body was looking at.

"NO WAY!"

'That's Alex Dright, the infamous Shepherd of Blood from the movie I watched last year.'

'In the movie, he's a star college football player by day and by night; he's a mass murderer who leaves his victims to die from blood loss.'

'I actually got transmigrated into this shitty slasher film; what a waste of a transmigration.'

'Well, I'm not gonna try looking for the killer; I'm nowhere strong enough or gutsy enough to do all that. I'll just leave town today, and it's basically a normal Earth, no need to fight.'

Jack changed out of his blood soaked clothes and into the best pair of shirt and pants he had in his suitcase. Well, it still left much to be desired since he was still homeless, but at least he wouldn't get kicked out of a restaurant if he went now.

Jack paused, and a thought came to mind.

'The same ability that let me analyse my changes also seems to be able to quantify my physical ability.'

Focusing inward, just like when he examined his body's changes, he recognised it. An internal value that represented his physical prowess. Right now he inherently understood that his physical was 1.2x higher than an average human.

'Wow, didn't expect that much of a jump from being half dead just because of a couple of adaptations within a few hours.'

Jack ran, jumped around, threw a couple of punches. Everything felt stronger, faster, lighter than his old body by a good margin. Not Olympic level, but a somewhat trained individual. 

He also checked the original body's savings. Only $22.17.

'Great, at this point I might die of starvation.'

So Jack started walking towards the town based on the extremely limited memory he received. As he walked, he couldn't help but notice that all the buildings looked like their older counterparts, and the cars on the road looked somewhat older-style as well.

'I can't tell just by looking; I should ask someone for the exact date when I get into town.'

Before long, Jack found the main road heading into Raven Hills. After walking for 30 minutes, he passed a few clusters of houses, driveways connecting to the main road. And finally, after walking up the hilly road, Jack saw the town. It looked like one of those mid-sized towns you'd pass on the highway to upstate New York. Without hesitation, Jack walked in, although it was a little weird walking on the side of a highway while cars passed by him.

Inside the town, Jack looked around. He spotted a general store, fire station, barber, and truck stop off in the distance, among others.

He flagged down the first person he saw. It was a middle-aged white man smoking a cigarette.

"Sorry to interrupt, sir. I'm Jack. Do you happen to know the date and time right now?"

The stranger just looked at Jack for a couple of seconds.

"You must not be from around here son."

"Doing drugs and forgetting which day it is?"

Jack's mouth twitched.

"Haha, no sir, no drugs over here. I'm actually travelling across the state on foot and lost track of time."

'Hopefully that's a believable lie. Even if it isn't, I doubt he'd question it.'

"On foot? Well, I wish you luck then son!"

"Anyways, it’s 12 p.m. on May 13, 2007!"

'2007!!'

'Wow, earlier than I thought'

"Thank you, sir, also if you wouldn't mind, could you point me towards the direction of the cheapest place to eat in this town?"

"Haha, hungry are ya? Don't worry, the food court just opened up for lunch; they got insanely low prices for the amount of food they give."

"It's a bit far if you're walking; tell ya what, I'll drop you off since I'm going the same way", He said as he pointed towards his black F150.

After the drive, Jack thanked the man and walked into the food court. It was bigger than he expected, with shops lined up along the outer walls with a seating area in the middle.

He picked the one that looked like it was giving the most food and got two portions of teriyaki chicken and rice.

'I can't believe it's only 3 dollars per portion, and the portions are big too. I would have to pay 20 dollars minimum back in my old world.'

Jack put his thoughts aside and started wolfing down the food. He didn't realise just how hungry he was until the first bite. Soon the first portion was finished, and as he was eating the second portion, he sensed something changing inside him. When he focused inwards, shock appeared on his face.

'Just eating brought my physical from 1.2x to 1.3x average human.'

'Now that I think about it, my body was probably being held back by the time I woke up this morning; if there's no food in my stomach, then there's nothing to build muscle with. When I started eating, combined with the ability of rapid bodily changes, my muscles started growing again.'

'But this growth will most likely only last until I've achieved my new natural baseline from all the adaptations yesterday.'

Just then, he heard some interesting local news on the TV playing above one of the shops.

"An unfortunate father, John Webbermen, fell victim to the 'Shepherd of Blood'. He was found dead from stabbing and blood loss, making him the 8th victim."

"Any conclusive information about the killer, either his location or identity, will be rewarded with $250. Furthermore, if the killer is captured, then a cash prize of $10,000 will be awarded by a group of the victim's families."

At first, Jack didn't really care about the murderer. Sure, he felt slightly indignant that he was stabbed, but that was nowhere near enough to make Jack face a bona fide mass murderer. However, everything changed when they mentioned the cash prize.

He looked at his remaining $16.17.

Then he looked at the mountain of food he wanted to order.

And finally, he looked at the local news again.

'The information reward isn't going to do anything; if I'm going to do this, then I might as well go for the big one.'

'I already knew who the killer was. Alex Dright, the college football player who was about to go pro.'

'In the movie, he dies because industrial-grade hydrochloric acid accidentally falls on him, giving the MC of the movie enough time to finish the job.'

'But I know where and when he's alone, so setting an ambush and capturing him alive should be easy enough.'

'I need a place to sleep for the night now, since Alex doesn't kill indoors.'

'But I only have around 16 dollars left; where am I going to find a room that cheap?'

'Maybe the truck stop I passed when I first got here; they should have bunkrooms since this place is next to a major highway.'

Jack made his way to the truck stop, paid 15 dollars to stay 8 hours. He was surprised when they didn't ask him for any ID or even if he was a trucker; they just led him to a tiny room with 4 bunk beds, 2 of which were already occupied by sleeping truckers. 

Jack lay down and let his mind wander about all the things that happened to him since yesterday. He still had a hard time believing everything that had happened was real.

As he drifted off to sleep, a few thoughts came to mind.

'Tomorrow I need to buy the key item that'll allow me to capture Alex, but I need around 30 dollars for that. Well, it seems like tomorrow's problem.'

[May 14, 5 am]

Jack woke up, and instead of feeling groggy, he felt extremely refreshed, as if he'd had the best sleep of his life.

As he stood up, Jack noticed that he felt a lot lighter and had more control over his body. When he felt his physical, he was shocked by how much higher the number had gotten.

